# The console image's build context: './wb.sh console' builds
# console/Dockerfile from the workbench's root — the package is a path
# dependency beside the console — and this is what goes in — the console and the package it depends on, nothing else. Not
# the workspaces, not git, not what Mix and the checks wrote, not the
# tests, and not a cartridge's papers: the console reads those off the
# mount at run time (Console.Papers, and the package's version/0 and
# need/0 read the cartridge's directory), so editing one costs no build.
# console_sources_hash in wb.sh hashes this same set to name the image:
# keep the two lists in step.
*
!console
!igniter
console/_build
console/deps
console/cover
console/doc
console/tmp
console/test
console/erl_crash.dump
console/priv/plts
console/priv/static/assets/js
console/priv/static/cache_manifest.json
console/assets/node_modules
igniter/_build
igniter/deps
igniter/test
igniter/erl_crash.dump
igniter/priv/plts
igniter/lib/workbench_igniter/features/*/README.md
igniter/lib/workbench_igniter/features/*/NEED.md
igniter/lib/workbench_igniter/features/*/DESIGN.md
igniter/lib/workbench_igniter/features/*/CHANGELOG.md
**/_archived
